//BUG="FEEDBACK.md 1.1 — && and || share a precedence tier"
//OUT="1 1 1"

// The same bug as 00, in the three shapes where the grouping actually changes
// the answer: a true left operand followed by an && that is false. With C
// precedence all three are 1; with the single shared tier, folded left to
// right, all three are 0.
//
// Note that most combinations give the same answer either way — for instance
// `false && false || true` is 1 under both readings — which is why this is so
// easy to miss in casual testing.

fn main
    out "{true || false && false} {true || true && false} {false || true || false && false}"
